\ {x}^{2}-36 & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the corresponding parabola given by $\\,y={x}^{2}-36\\,$ and find its roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-36 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-{6}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (x-6)(x+6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the roots are $x=\\pm 6.$ \n\nSolving the inequality ${x}^{2}-36>0$ is equivalent to finding the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y={x}^{2}-36$ is above the $x$-axis (where $y>0$).\n\nSince the leading coefficient of the quadratic expression is positive, the parabola opens upward. Therefore, the solution set lies outside the roots (but it does not include them), as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965374/assets/6f8d7de374bf83e33a9b8d608df0fc1f3ea44937c1dda33485572067ec60c6e4.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-6)\\cup (6,\\infty ).$" 13194139534639 true] [17592186300462 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300463 13194139534639 true] [17592186300462 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300464 13194139534639 true] [17592186300462 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300465 13194139534639 true] [17592186300462 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300466 13194139534639 true] [17592186300462 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300467 13194139534639 true] [17592186300462 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534639 true] [17592186300462 1041 "selection" 13194139534639 true] [17592186300462 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300465 13194139534639 true] [17592186300462 1110 #uuid "b25a08e2-3b9f-5247-8a94-077865f4fa5c" 13194139534639 true] [17592186300463 1034 "x\\in (-6,6)" 13194139534639 true] [17592186300463 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534639 true] [17592186300463 1111 #uuid "72bdd43e-accf-5470-a959-e7531649aaa3" 13194139534639 true] [17592186300464 1034 "x\\in (-6,\\infty )" 13194139534639 true] [17592186300464 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534639 true] [17592186300464 1111 #uuid "12f0d2d7-68c7-5100-aa32-baec9f3b01c6" 13194139534639 true] [17592186300465 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,-6)\\cup (6,\\infty )" 13194139534639 true] [17592186300465 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534639 true] [17592186300465 1111 #uuid "04a9dcf8-d644-5a88-bdf2-7fe1678aaa42" 13194139534639 true] [17592186300466 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,-6)" 13194139534639 true] [17592186300466 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534639 true] [17592186300466 1111 #uuid "87f303fc-02a3-52d3-ae2a-cc920d6ebcba" 13194139534639 true] [17592186300467 1034 "x\\in (6,\\infty )" 13194139534639 true] [17592186300467 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534639 true] [17592186300467 1111 #uuid "74d13465-a496-541d-91fe-de8de63aa7c7" 13194139534639 true] [17592186300468 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300469 13194139534639 true] [17592186300468 1089 "q-70261" 13194139534639 true] [17592186300468 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534639 true] [17592186300468 1100 "Solve the inequality  ${x}^{2}\\ge 25$ using a graphical method." 13194139534639 true] [17592186300468 1113 #uuid "3d89b451-9545-5819-adbe-c21aafa486b0" 13194139534639 true] [17592186300468 1145 "Bringing all the terms to the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\ge 25 \\\\ {x}^{2}-25 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the corresponding parabola given by $\\,y={x}^{2}-25\\,$ and find its roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-25 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-{5}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (x-5)(x+5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the roots are $x=\\pm 5.$ \n\nSolving the inequality ${x}^{2}-25\\ge 0$ is equivalent to finding the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y={x}^{2}-25$ is above or intersects the $x$-axis (where $y\\ge 0$).\n\nSince the leading coefficient of the quadratic expression is positive, the parabola opens upward. Therefore, the solution set lies outside the roots (including them), as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965374/assets/77c4caaa90dc3978ab6590885113a7e4ac0d155d3c2082166ab91c70603b0ea0.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-5]\\cup [5,\\infty ).$" 13194139534639 true] [175